{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T11:01:03.412Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1b0e5123829f6bd0f819a465","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:01:03.376Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Pre-gate adversarial review found a real ownership gap: copying the global close episode onto an untouched admitted member could make a peer edit look like an owned forward mutation. A new real-process regression failed before the correction. The native admission hook now signs each exact target, operation, before-head and before/after document hashes under its native item lock, using an ephemeral Ed25519 key. The public key is anchored in registered intent; signed proposals are durably staged by the same host SDK in audited workspace settings before the item write, then frozen into native item history before compensation. The private key is never serialized. Copied episodes and same-author native closes now lack the required signed proposal and are preserved with typed partial receipts. The corrected regression passes; fresh signed-protocol focused tests passed 11/11. Earlier gates and revert proofs are interim evidence and will be refreshed for this design."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:01:03.412Z"}],"before_hash":"df5bc78fa5fb6b83b0eda7e9b64185790505e3a492953c9af907c860c5d6dbc4","after_hash":"9a296603df5b167abdcbd4a4a8a851b8ed1984c4b710a9dc46b592d677d7f047","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a90f905779b609170799bf7a526cdd06fa79cf81f428b2e0d048397a4407f9a2"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T11:07:53.778Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1b0e5123829f6bd0f819a465","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:07:53.705Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"The signed-proposal design is now exercised through the pinned pm runner: its eight linked real-tracker regressions passed with the updated timeout. Exact signed proposals also bind unlogged bytes and native SDK history; a copied episode on an untouched member no longer authorizes rollback. Pending compensation validates its complete frozen post-close heads before any restore. Current signature, history-outage, Plan-policy and privacy checks are being measured before the full npm/Bun gates; no claim of final coverage or CI is made yet."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:07:53.778Z"}],"before_hash":"9a296603df5b167abdcbd4a4a8a851b8ed1984c4b710a9dc46b592d677d7f047","after_hash":"37c6bced6174f0e68301317520e6ba97fa2d108f45200733d0b179e12a752901","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"df081780b390c92d968e03a12dfb33c17847173553e0b12dfc351400d0b7cd11"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T11:36:09.120Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1b0e5123829f6bd0f819a465","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/9","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:36:09.072Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Signed-protocol behavioral reverts in disposable copies are complete: original close failed 56 of 58 tests; targeted cleanup, member resume, signed ownership, frozen post heads, dependency fences, missing restore receipt, signature validation, persisted intent validation and delete-proposal guards each fail when weakened. Restored implementation passed 9 selected critical tests. A native dependent-policy warning also reproduced a compensation admission failure; compensation now drops uncommitted success warnings instead of re-emitting rejected content. Its real-SDK regression passes and an isolated function revert is being verified. Starting unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release gates with fresh home and no global Git identity; earlier aggregate coverage and packed runs remain interim evidence."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T11:36:09.120Z"}],"before_hash":"37c6bced6174f0e68301317520e6ba97fa2d108f45200733d0b179e12a752901","after_hash":"427c2613fb1220fb07dfa47d9837cba635aac4f1638e2aaca4555ffb92f11bb8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ca5885a91a8457d